== Strategy ==
* The '''UFO Toilet''' comes out at Wave 20, killing many unsuspecting players. You should plan ahead to make sure that you are able to defeat this enemy.
* In [[Hard Mode|Hard Mode,]] the UFO Toilet can get very far and stun many [[Units|units.]]
* You should not spend all of your money on [[Medic Cameraman|Medic Cameraman.]] Instead, the [[Scientist Cameraman|Scientist Cameramen]] and [[Santa TV Man|Santa Tv]] can block the UFO Toilet's stuns. 
* If you know you cannot defeat it, you can let it leak as it does 300 damage, leaving you with 100 Health. 
* If it gets too far and you know you do not have enough damage to take it, you can place down a [[Secret Agent]] that can do 100,000 Damage to it. However, if UFO Toilet stuns it or goes invisible, Secret Agent will be wasted.
* [[Astro Upgraded Titan Cameraman]] can slow down UFO Toilet, same for [[Green Laser Cameraman]] and [[TV Woman]] as UFO Toilet is a fast enemy.
* High DPS Units are recommended to take this down, such as [[Jetpack Cameraman|Future Large Clock Man,]] but do not spend too much if you know you cannot defeat it.
* As this enemy is fast, you can use [[Mech Cameraman]] or Level 5/6 [[Upgraded Titan Cameraman]], the latter also doing high DPS to '''UFO Toilet'''. [[TV Woman]] is not recommended as it does low DPS with low radius and will eeasily be stunned.

== Trivia ==
* The UFO Toilet has a stronger variant called the [[Laser UFO Toilet]] which is released in the Episode 60 Update.
* The UFO Toilet used to be the final boss of [[Hard Mode]] before getting replaced by the [[Boss Toilet 3.0|Boss Toilet 3.0.]] (And it replaced the [[Flying Rocket Launcher Toilet]] as the final boss) my
